# ==============================================================================
# Static System Hostname Configuration
# ==============================================================================
# Purpose:
#   Sets the system's static hostname (short name, no domain part).
#   This is typically read by systemd-hostnamed and applied to the kernel's
#   hostname via hostnamectl or the init system.
#
# Constraints:
#   - Must contain only alphanumeric characters, hyphens, and dots.
#   - Typically limited to 64 characters.
#   - No fully qualified domain name (FQDN) should be included here;
#     that is handled by DNS, /etc/hosts, or NSS configuration.
#
# Usage:
#   This file is usually /etc/hostname on Linux systems.

# The system's static hostname.
# Defaults to 'localhost' if not provided by the playbook/role.
{{ hostname | default('localhost') }}